## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical system design for regulatory compliance in multilingual content environments, focusing on per-language calibration, privacy preservation, and safe deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual models with language-specific adapters
- Per-language risk calibration and drift detection mechanisms
- Privacy-preserving logging and active learning frameworks
- Gradual rollout, canary deployments, and automated rollback triggers

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing and scoring
function scoreContent(text) {
  const lang = detectLanguage(text);
  const adapter = getLanguageAdapter(lang);
  const riskScore = adapter.predict(text);
  return { language: lang, riskScore, decision: moderate(riskScore) };
}
```

## Why This Is Questioned

This question evaluates end-to-end system design with competing constraints: real-time performance, multilingual support, strict privacy requirements, and operational scalability across tenants.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming NLP
- On-device privacy preservation
- Multilingual ASR (Automatic Speech Recognition)
- Differential privacy (DP) embeddings
- Edge inference
- Model drift detection
- Human-in-the-loop annotation

## Code Example

```javascript
async function processAudioChunk(chunk, tenantId) {
  const text = await asrOnDevice(chunk, tenantId);
  const redacted = await redactPII(text, tenantId);
  const signal = await applyDifferentialPrivacy(redacted, tenantId);

  if (signal.riskScore > config.threshold) {
    await routeToTriageQueue(signal, tenantId);
  }
  return signal;
}
```

